      "text": "Tool calling needs SGLang with the minicpm5 tool-call parser (sgl-project/sglang#25600). The openbmb cookbook says to install SGLang from main because v0.5.12.post1 lacked it; the PyPI 0.5.20 wheel used here ships it, so no source build is needed any more. The model writes XML tool calls (<function name=\"x\"><param name=\"k\">v</param></function>) and they come back as OpenAI tool_calls with finish_reason tool_calls, with thinking on and off."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "SGLang has no MiniCPM5 reasoning parser, but the model uses plain <think> ... </think>, so --reasoning-parser qwen3 splits it into reasoning_content. With enable_thinking left unset the template adds no <think> prefix; the model opens the tag itself and the qwen3 parser still catches it."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "flashinfer JIT-compiles its prefill kernels on the first request and shells out to ninja. In a venv that is not activated the first prefill dies with FileNotFoundError: ninja and the scheduler exits; put the venv bin directory on PATH before starting the server."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "In a llama.cpp deployment the card warns that the default min_p 0.05 causes repetition and asks for min_p 0; the SGLang default min_p is already 0."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "SGLang RadixAttention reuses any cached prefix and has no per-request switch to skip it, and the prefill, long-context and serving workloads reuse the same prompts and haystacks. To keep prefill cold without turning the cache off for the whole server, the speed and long-context rows went through a small proxy on the box that prepends a unique HTML comment (<!-- 12 hex chars -->, about 12 tokens) to the first message of every request, so the shared prefix is only the few chat-template tokens before it. Input token counts include the comment."
    }
  ],
